BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bees: A Story of Survival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T100000
UID:61e79956b771c15d15493a210ed0a375@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Bringing some buzz into your summer. Journey into the world of
  bees in a stunning new immersive experience that brings together the beau
 ty of art with the power of science. Created by the National Museums Liver
 pool in partnership with award-winning artist and sculptor\, Wolfgang Butt
 ress\, the exhibition highlights 120-million years of bee adaptation and s
 urvival\, telling the epic tale of these incredible creatures and their re
 lationship to us and the natural world. Based on science and full of imagi
 nation\, the experiential exhibition presents a fusion of nature\, art\, m
 usic\, and architecture that transports visitors into the world of bees - 
 from the tiny\, fascinating anatomy of a single bee and the magical wonder
  of honey bee colonies to the important roles bees play in our lives and t
 he everyday threats they face. Through immersive environments\, art instal
 lations\, soundscapes\, and more\, learn about the life of bees and the wo
 rld they inhabit.
LOCATION:Royal Ontario Museum\, 100 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/exhibitions/bees-story-survival?utm_sou
 rce=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=bees
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yacht Rock Show Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T193000
UID:cb1511fd75b621bcf7a90bf8c714fed9@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Yacht Rock Show Canada is an authentic tribute to the 70s 
 and 80s Classic Smooth Rock Era that defined a generation. Experience an u
 nforgettable musical voyage\, dancing and listening to classic hits from a
 rtists including: Toto\, Styx\, The Doobie Brothers\, Michael McDonald\, C
 hristopher Cross\, Kenny Loggins\, Steely Dan\, Boz Scaggs\, Player\, Litt
 le River Band\, Ambrosia. The El Mocambo is a legendary live music and ent
 ertainment venue in Toronto\, Canada\, that has hosted countless world-fam
 ous artists since it opened in 1948\, including The Rolling Stones\, Elvis
  Costello\, Blondie\, The Ramones\, and Stevie Ray Vaughan. The new El Moc
 ambo features state-of-the-art sound and lighting\, a recording studio\, a
 nd multiple floors for events and performances\, offering a modern\, VIP l
 ive music experience while maintaining its historical significance.
LOCATION:The El Mocambo\, 464 Spadina Ave\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://buy.pressplaytickets.com/yrs-elmo/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
