BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gather for Doors Open at Spadina Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T100000
UID:cdab6988cbeb33bce938c6377a08a903@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Spadina Museum tells the stories of the affluent Austin family
 \, those who worked in their service\, and of the transformational changes
  in Toronto in the 1920s. At Spadina Museum visitors are invited to engage
  with the site at their own pace and to bring their questions and curiosit
 y. This year's theme for Doors Open is The World in a City and at Spadina 
 Museum visitors will find elements of gathering\, sports and play througho
 ut\, exploring the sports\, games and leisure activities enjoyed in the 19
 20s. Visitors are invited to enjoy the 6 acres of lush gardens surrounding
  the home.
LOCATION:Spadina Museum\, 285 Spadina Rd\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/spadi
 na-museum/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Prepare The Ground 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T180000
UID:46151d6f6f7fcea51fe1ece528fa554c@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:A community-led arts and heavy music festival\, the first of i
 ts kind in the city! Founded by two lifelong friends\, Toronto-based conce
 rt promoter Denholm Whale and KW Campol of music management company Mythos
  and the Perpetual Flame Ministries record label/art house. Drawing inspir
 ation from European festival stalwarts like Roadburn\, Supersonic\, and Am
 plifest\, we're focused on heavy music as an ethos of collective catharsis
  more than a dedication to one specific metal subgenre. From burgeoning ar
 tists\, to favorites you never thought would reunite\, to one-off full alb
 um sets\, a heavily curated and meticulously planned lineup is the festiva
 l's key component.
LOCATION:Trinity St Paul's\, 427 Bloor St W\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://link.dice.fm/u82686a23a97?dice_id=u82686a23a97
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
